iktionary.org/wiki/plus#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:528361172a0fcbab82","definition":"To add; to subject to addition.","example":"For him y is a unique number, like 7, but for the time being unknown — if one does the operation of 'plussing 4' one still has, as a result, a unique number even though one does not yet know what it is.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":["add","addition","times"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:29fa6220616e155f2d","definition":"To increase in magnitude.","example":"I am doing a lot of writing here, plussing the script, adding sequences.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"often","register":"often","wordFamily":["add","addition","times"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7e0b47912aefc8595a","definition":"To improve.","example":"Coach Wooden didn't have to depend upon having the most talented players on his team because he could depend upon plussing to constantly make everyone better.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["add","addition","times"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8d0740c3059c4b16bc","definition":"To provide critical feedback by giving suggestions for improvement rather than criticisms.","example":"The animators and directors on the receiving end of the plussing don't necessarily have to accept and incorporate the feedback, but plussing provides a method to share criticisms in a way that makes it more likely that they will.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["add","addition","times"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e5910d9c861e7910f7","definition":"To sell additional related items with an original purchase.","example":"Good will is also secured by plussing the original purchase with another article that goes appropriately with it.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["add","addition","times"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2ec9293268621484d9","definition":"To frame in a positive light; to provide a sympathetic interpretation.","example":"Plussing is a technique for enhancing a positive atmosphere in the session, for diminishing hostility, and for raising self-esteem.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["add","addition","times"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f769522741b09b14f3","definition":"To give a mark of approval on Google+.","example":"How do you get others to add you or your brand to their circles? By creating and sharing useful content, commenting, plussing others' content and comments, and engaging with others on Google+.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["add","addition","times"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https:/